Notebook[{Cell["Lepton-quark and lepton-gluon scattering with a different \
tagged parton, step 3: phase-space integrals", "Title"], 
  Cell["Input: Results/<route>/Algebra.wl from step 2 (choose the route \
below).  Output: Results/<route>/Reduced.wl with the real-emission \
phase-space integrals of both channels evaluated as Laurent series in eps, \
exact in the threshold variable.  Both spin cases are treated \
together.\n\nMethod, as in Processes/LeptonQuark/3-Reduce.wl (read its \
introduction first): the unobserved two-particle phase space of lp and r is \
written as cut propagators, Kira reduces the integrals to the two-body volume \
and one angular master per family, and the masters are evaluated as Euler \
integrals with SubTropica.  The denominators of the squared matrix elements \
are, besides the photon propagator tau = (k - p - r)^2 = a + b + t,\n\n  l q \
-> l g q:    t = (k - p)^2 (fixed) and b = (p + r)^2:   family \
real_b_tau[1,1,nb,nt] = integral of 1/(b^nb tau^nt),\n  l g -> l q qbar: t \
and a = (k - r)^2:                           family real_a_tau[1,1,na,nt] = \
integral of 1/(a^na tau^nt),\n\n(indices 1 and 2 are the cut propagators), so \
no partial fractions are needed: each channel lives in one family.  The \
invariant a (or b) that is not a denominator of the channel is written as tau \
- b - t (or tau - a - t).  The hatted invariant spe3 of the polarized matrix \
elements becomes a dimension shift as in the lepton-quark process.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load", "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["route = \"FeynCalc\";        (* \"FeynCalc\", \"FORM\" or \"Tracer\": \
which step-2 result to reduce *)\nalgebra = LoadResult[\"Algebra\", \
route];\nspins = {\"Unpolarized\", \"Polarized\"};\nchannels = {\"QG\", \
\"GQ\"};\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Real emission: terms of the two families", "Section"], 
  Cell["Remove the common factors (CF or TR, ee^4 eq^2 gs^2), write D = 4 - 2 \
eps and u = s4 - s - t, express the matrix element through the two \
denominators of its family, and read off the integrals: a term x^(-i) y^(-j) \
with x, y the two denominators is the family integral with indices {1, 1, i, \
j} (negative indices are numerators).  The coefficients are rational in s, t, \
s4 and eps (the gluon average 1/(D-2) of the second channel makes them \
rational in eps) and polynomial in spe3.", "Text"], 
  Cell["familyOf = <|\"QG\" -> {KRealBTau, b, tau, a -> tau - b - t}, \"GQ\" \
-> {KRealATau, a, tau, b -> tau - a - t}|>;\ncolourOf = <|\"QG\" -> CF, \
\"GQ\" -> TR|>;\n(* The two channels already have two denominators. Map each \
additive fraction\n   directly to two inert forms; keep its scalar \
denominator independent. *)\ntoFamilyForms[expr_, {head_, x_, y_, rule_}] := \
Module[{mapped},\n  mapped = MapIntegrationDenominators[expr, {rule}, {x, y}, \
Function[factor,\n    Which[Expand[factor - x] === 0, fX, Expand[factor + x] \
=== 0, -fX,\n      Expand[factor - y] === 0, fY, Expand[factor + y] === 0, \
-fY,\n      True, Require[False, \"A denominator is not one of the two family \
forms\", factor]]]];\n  Require[!FailureQ[mapped], \"Termwise family \
conversion failed\", mapped];\n  mapped /. {x -> fX, y -> fY}];\nrowVariables \
= {fX, fY, spe3};\nreconstructUnit[term_, rows_List] := Together[Total[\n  \
#[\"Coefficient\"] spe3^#[\"HatPower\"] fX^(-#[\"Integral\"][[3]]) \
fY^(-#[\"Integral\"][[4]]) & /@ rows] - term] === \
0;\nmakeFamilyConverter[head_] := With[{familyHead = head},\n  \
CreateIntegralRowConverter[rowVariables, Function[unit, Module[{powers, \
rows},\n    powers = Exponent[unit, #] & /@ rowVariables;\n    \
Require[VectorQ[powers, IntegerQ] && Last[powers] >= 0, \"Unsupported family \
monomial\", unit];\n    rows = {<|\"Integral\" -> familyHead[1, 1, \
-powers[[1]], -powers[[2]]],\n      \"HatPower\" -> powers[[3]], \
\"Coefficient\" -> 1|>};\n    Require[reconstructUnit[unit, rows], \"A unit \
family mapping does not reconstruct\", unit]; rows]], \
reconstructUnit]];\nfamilyConverters = Association @ Table[channel -> \
makeFamilyConverter[familyOf[channel][[1]]], {channel, \
channels}];\nrealStripped = Association @ Table[channel -> Association @ \
Table[spin ->\n  Expand[algebra[\"Real\"][channel][spin]/(colourOf[channel] \
ee^4 eq^2 gs^2) /.\n    {D -> 4 - 2 eps, u -> s4 - s - t}], {spin, spins}], \
{channel, channels}];\nrowInputs = Association @ Table[channel -> Association \
@ Table[spin ->\n  \
CombineLaurentTerms[toFamilyForms[realStripped[channel][spin], \
familyOf[channel]], rowVariables],\n  {spin, spins}], {channel, \
channels}];\nRequire[FreeQ[rowInputs, _Failure], \"Laurent coefficient \
grouping failed\", rowInputs];\nrealRowResults = Association @ Table[channel \
-> Association @ Table[spin ->\n  \
familyConverters[channel][rowInputs[channel][spin]], {spin, spins}], \
{channel, channels}];\nRequire[FreeQ[realRowResults, _Failure], \
\"Integral-row conversion failed\", realRowResults];\nrealTerms = Association \
@ Table[channel -> Association @ Table[spin ->\n  \
realRowResults[channel][spin][\"Rows\"], {spin, spins}], {channel, \
channels}];\nallRows = Flatten[Table[realTerms[channel][spin], {channel, \
channels}, {spin, spins}]];\nindexRanges = <|\"denominators\" -> \
Max[Prepend[Total[Select[List @@ #[\"Integral\"], # > 0 &]] & /@ allRows, \
0]],\n  \"numerators\" -> Max[Prepend[-Total[Select[List @@ #[\"Integral\"], \
# < 0 &]] & /@ allRows, 0]]|>;\nRequire[indexRanges[\"denominators\"] <= 7 && \
indexRanges[\"numerators\"] <= 3,\n  \"The integrals exceed the shipped Kira \
index ranges\", indexRanges];\nDataset[realTerms[\"QG\"][\"Polarized\"]]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Check that the terms add up to the matrix element.", 
   "Text"], Cell["rebuild[rows_, {head_, x_, y_, rule_}] := \
Total[#[\"Coefficient\"] spe3^#[\"HatPower\"] x^(-#[\"Integral\"][[3]]) \
y^(-#[\"Integral\"][[4]]) & /@ \
rows];\nDo[Require[Together[(realStripped[channel][spin] /. \
familyOf[channel][[4]]) - rebuild[realTerms[channel][spin], \
familyOf[channel]]] === 0,\n  \"The family terms do not add up to the matrix \
element\", {channel, spin}], {channel, channels}, {spin, spins}];\n\"family \
terms verified\"", "Input"], Cell["Reduction with Kira", "Section"], 
  Cell["The YAML files in kira/real define the two families (the same \
definitions as in the lepton-quark process); the target list is written from \
the integrals that occur.  Kira sets s = 1 (symbol_to_replace_by_one); \
RestoreScale puts the scale back.", "Text"], Cell["kiraNames = {KRealATau -> \
\"real_a_tau\", KRealBTau -> \"real_b_tau\"};\nreferenceRealMasters = \
{KRealATau[1, 1, 0, 0], KRealBTau[1, 1, 0, 0], KRealATau[1, 1, 1, 1], \
KRealBTau[1, 1, 1, 1]};\nrealTargets = \
Union[Flatten[Table[Lookup[realTerms[channel][spin], \"Integral\"], {channel, \
channels}, {spin, spins}]], referenceRealMasters];\nkiraReal = \
PrepareKira[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"kira\", \"real\"}], \
FileNameJoin[{ResultsDirectory[route], \"kira\", \
\"real\"}]];\nWriteKiraTargets[kiraReal, realTargets, \
kiraNames];\nrealTargets", "Input"], Cell["RunKira[kiraReal];\nrealRules = \
RestoreScale[Join @@ Table[KiraRules[kiraReal, name, kiraNames],\n  {name, \
Select[{\"real_a_tau\", \"real_b_tau\"},\n    \
FileExistsQ[FileNameJoin[{kiraReal, \"results\", #, \"kira_targets.m\"}]] \
&]}],\n  s, {t -> t/s, s4 -> s4/s}, {KRealATau, \
KRealBTau}];\nCheckReductionCoverage[realTargets, realRules, {KRealATau, \
KRealBTau}, referenceRealMasters];\nColumn[realRules]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Every integral reduces to the phase-space volume (real_a_tau[1,1,0,0] \
or real_b_tau[1,1,0,0], the same integral) and the angular integrals \
real_a_tau[1,1,1,1] and real_b_tau[1,1,1,1].  A term with spe3^n uses the \
rules at d = 4 + 2n - 2 eps; KiraMaster[family, indices, shift] denotes a \
master in D + shift dimensions.", "Text"], Cell["masterHeads = {KRealATau -> \
\"real_a_tau\", KRealBTau -> \"real_b_tau\"};\nreduce[rows_] := \
Collect[Expand[Total[Map[Function[row, With[{n = row[\"HatPower\"]},\n  \
row[\"Coefficient\"] (4 Pi)^n (-1)^n Pochhammer[-eps, n] *\n    \
((row[\"Integral\"] /. realRules /. d -> 4 + 2 n - 2 eps) /.\n      (head : \
KRealATau | KRealBTau)[indices__] :> KiraMaster[head /. masterHeads, \
{indices}, 2 n])]], rows]]], _KiraMaster, Together];\nrealReduced = \
Association @ Table[channel -> Association @ Table[spin -> \
reduce[realTerms[channel][spin]], {spin, spins}], {channel, \
channels}];\nRequire[FreeQ[realReduced, KRealATau | KRealBTau], \"Some \
integrals were not reduced\"];\nUnion[Cases[realReduced, _KiraMaster, \
Infinity]]", "Input"], Cell["Master integrals", "Section"], 
  Cell["The same masters as in the lepton-quark process, with the same \
checks: the two-body volume Phi2 (and its D + 2 version) and the angular \
integral\n\n   Omega(z) = 2 (1-2eps) integral_0^infinity dx x^(-1-eps) \
(1+x)^eps/(z+x),\n\nwritten with the connection formula that separates the \
branch z^(-1-eps) from the regular hypergeometric function F1(z) = \
2F1(1,1;2+eps;z) (and F2 in D + 2 dimensions):\n\n   Omega(z) = -2 \
(1-2eps)/eps [ Gamma(1-eps) Gamma(1+eps) (1-z)^eps z^(-1-eps) + Gamma(1-eps) \
Gamma(-1-eps)/Gamma(-eps)^2 F1(z) ],\n   Omega2(z) = 2 (3-2eps)/(1-eps) [ \
Gamma(2-eps) Gamma(eps) (1-z)^(eps-1) z^(-eps) + Gamma(2-eps) \
Gamma(-eps)/Gamma(1-eps)^2 F2(z) ].\n\nIn these channels the cross ratios zAT \
and zBT tend to 1 at the threshold w = 1 (there is no soft-gluon singularity: \
the gluon is observed or absent), so no plus distributions arise; the branch \
(1-z)^eps combines with s4^(-eps) of the volume into logarithms of 1 - w.  F1 \
and F2 are evaluated as Euler integrals with SubTropica and kept as inert \
symbols F1[n][z], F2[n][z] (the coefficients of eps^n) until step 4.", 
   "Text"], Cell["LoadSubTropica[]", "Input"], 
  Cell["masters = <|\n  \"phaseSpace\" -> EulerIntegral[1/Gamma[1 - eps], \
x^(-eps) (1 + x)^(2 eps - 2), {x}, {}, 2, eps],\n  \"phaseSpaceD2\" -> \
EulerIntegral[1/Gamma[2 - eps], x^(1 - eps) (1 + x)^(2 eps - 4), {x}, {}, 1, \
eps],\n  \"F1\" -> EulerIntegral[1 + eps, (1 + y)^(-1 - eps)/(1 + zb y), {y}, \
{zb}, 2, eps] /. zb -> 1 - z,\n  \"F2\" -> EulerIntegral[eps, (1 + \
y)^(-eps)/(1 + zb y), {y}, {zb}, 2, eps] /. zb -> 1 - z|>", "Input"], 
  Cell["check[x_] := Require[Simplify[x] === 0, \"Master integral check \
failed\", x];\ncheck[Normal[Series[masters[\"phaseSpace\"] - Gamma[1 - \
eps]/Gamma[2 - 2 eps], {eps, 0, \
2}]]];\ncheck[Normal[Series[masters[\"phaseSpaceD2\"] - Gamma[2 - \
eps]/Gamma[4 - 2 eps], {eps, 0, 1}]]];\ntruncationCheck[series_, exact_, \
power_] := Module[{d1, d2},\n  d1 = N[(exact - series) /. {eps -> -1/50, z -> \
1/3}, 30];\n  d2 = N[(exact - series) /. {eps -> -1/100, z -> 1/3}, 30];\n  \
Require[Abs[d2/d1 - 2^-power] < 2^-power/10, \"Master integral disagrees with \
its closed form\", {d1, d2}]; {d1, d2}];\ntruncationCheck[masters[\"F1\"], \
Hypergeometric2F1[1, 1, 2 + eps, z], 3];\ntruncationCheck[masters[\"F2\"], \
Hypergeometric2F1[1, 1, 1 + eps, z], 3]", "Input"], 
  Cell["angular[zz_] := -2 (1 - 2 eps)/eps (Gamma[1 - eps] Gamma[1 + eps] (1 \
- zz)^eps zz^(-1 - eps) +\n  Gamma[1 - eps] Gamma[-1 - eps]/Gamma[-eps]^2 \
Sum[eps^n F1[n][zz], {n, 0, 2}]);\nangularD2[zz_] := 2 (3 - 2 eps)/(1 - eps) \
(Gamma[2 - eps] Gamma[eps] (1 - zz)^(eps - 1) zz^(-eps) +\n  Gamma[2 - eps] \
Gamma[-eps]/Gamma[1 - eps]^2 Sum[eps^n F2[n][zz], {n, 0, \
2}]);\nmasterFunctions = Join[{F1[0][0] -> 1, F2[0][0] -> 1, F1[_][0] -> 0, \
F2[_][0] -> 0},\n  Table[F1[n][zz_] :> \
Evaluate[SeriesCoefficient[masters[\"F1\"], {eps, 0, n}] /. z -> zz], {n, 0, \
2}],\n  Table[F2[n][zz_] :> Evaluate[SeriesCoefficient[masters[\"F2\"], {eps, \
0, n}] /. z -> zz], {n, 0, 2}]];\nnumericCheck[expr_, integrand_, power_] := \
Module[{d1, d2},\n  d1 = N[expr /. {eps -> -1/40, z -> 1/3}, 20] - \
NIntegrate[integrand /. {eps -> -1/40, z -> 1/3}, {x, 0, Infinity}, \
WorkingPrecision -> 30];\n  d2 = N[expr /. {eps -> -1/80, z -> 1/3}, 20] - \
NIntegrate[integrand /. {eps -> -1/80, z -> 1/3}, {x, 0, Infinity}, \
WorkingPrecision -> 30];\n  Require[Abs[d2/d1 - 2^-power] < 2^-power/10, \
\"Angular master disagrees with direct integration\", {d1, d2}]; {d1, \
d2}];\nnumericCheck[angular[z] /. masterFunctions, 2 (1 - 2 eps) x^(-1 - eps) \
(1 + x)^eps/(z + x), 3];\nnumericCheck[angularD2[z] /. masterFunctions, 2 (3 \
- 2 eps) x^(-eps) (1 + x)^(eps - 1)/(z + x), 2]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Insert the physical masters", "Section"], 
  Cell["Normalization as in the lepton-quark process: Phi2 = (4 Pi)^eps \
s4^(-eps)/(8 Pi) Gamma(1-eps)/Gamma(2-2eps) for the measure d^D r/(2 \
Pi)^(D-1) delta+(r^2) 2 Pi delta+((pRec - r)^2), Phi2' = (4 Pi)^(eps-1) \
s4^(1-eps)/(8 Pi) Gamma(2-eps)/Gamma(4-2eps) in D + 2 dimensions, and the \
angular masters Phi2 Omega(z) divided by the product of the two invariants at \
the symmetric point, with the cross ratios\n\n   zAT = -t \
(s+t-s4)/((s+t)(s4-t)),   zBT = -s t/((s-s4)(s4-t)).", "Text"], 
  Cell["phaseSpace = (4 Pi)^eps s4^(-eps)/(8 Pi) \
masters[\"phaseSpace\"];\nphaseSpaceD2 = (4 Pi)^(eps - 1) s4^(1 - eps)/(8 Pi) \
masters[\"phaseSpaceD2\"];\nzAT = -t (s + t - s4)/((s + t) (s4 - t));  zBT = \
-s t/((s - s4) (s4 - t));\nphysicalMasters = {\n  KiraMaster[\"real_a_tau\", \
{1, 1, 0, 0}, 0] -> phaseSpace,\n  KiraMaster[\"real_b_tau\", {1, 1, 0, 0}, \
0] -> phaseSpace,\n  KiraMaster[\"real_a_tau\", {1, 1, 1, 1}, 0] -> \
phaseSpace angular[zAT]/((s + t) (s4 - t)),\n  KiraMaster[\"real_b_tau\", {1, \
1, 1, 1}, 0] -> -phaseSpace angular[zBT]/((s - s4) (s4 - t)),\n  \
KiraMaster[\"real_a_tau\", {1, 1, 0, 0}, 2] -> phaseSpaceD2,\n  \
KiraMaster[\"real_b_tau\", {1, 1, 0, 0}, 2] -> phaseSpaceD2,\n  \
KiraMaster[\"real_a_tau\", {1, 1, 1, 1}, 2] -> phaseSpaceD2 \
angularD2[zAT]/((s + t) (s4 - t)),\n  KiraMaster[\"real_b_tau\", {1, 1, 1, \
1}, 2] -> -phaseSpaceD2 angularD2[zBT]/((s - s4) (s4 - t))};\nrealIntegrated \
= Association @ Table[channel -> Association @ Table[spin ->\n  \
colourOf[channel] ee^4 eq^2 gs^2 (realReduced[channel][spin] /. \
physicalMasters), {spin, spins}], {channel, \
channels}];\nRequire[FreeQ[realIntegrated, KiraMaster], \"A master integral \
was not inserted\"];\nKeys[realIntegrated]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Save", "Section"], Cell["reduced = <|\"Real\" -> realIntegrated, \
\"Masters\" -> masters, \"MasterFunctions\" -> masterFunctions, \"RealRules\" \
-> realRules, \"Route\" -> route|>;\nSaveResult[\"Reduced\", reduced, \
route];\nKeys[reduced]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
